From: mscharged-port native source preparation
Subject: [PATCH] Keep native CPU decoder safe points outside graphics presentation
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

The actual source movie path exposed full VI output servicing inside a CPU
MCU decode. A native render worker could then wait for a Wayland swapchain
image while its event owner was inside the decoder. Use the existing native
owner-only hardware endpoint at this stable CPU boundary, as GPU waits do.
It preserves real source audio/input delivery, owner, mask and reentrancy
rules without invoking VI output or nested presentation. Existing main/swap
hardware boundaries still service the real VI clock and its callbacks.
No codec equation, output bytes, source movie timing or mixing is changed.

diff --git a/lib/dolphin/thp/THPDec.cpp b/lib/dolphin/thp/THPDec.cpp
--- a/lib/dolphin/thp/THPDec.cpp
+++ b/lib/dolphin/thp/THPDec.cpp
@@ -613,7 +613,7 @@
       // A completed MCU is a stable boundary between entropy/IDCT/output work;
       // the host endpoint preserves owner, mask and reentrancy rules. No codec
       // state, equations, source playback decisions or callback are replaced.
-      aurora_service_hardware();
+      aurora_service_hardware_owner();
 #endif
 
       if (context.restartInterval != 0 && ++restartCount == context.restartInterval) {
